  "scope": "One fresh harness-owned Kind v0.32.0 / Kubernetes v1.36.1 cluster, with Kind's default CNI disabled and Cilium 1.20.5 installed from the checked OCI chart archive. The case verifies the chart and Cilium agent/operator image pins, then checks one TCP marker request between two case-owned pods in the cluster. A deliberately invalid readiness-probe threshold is submitted through Helm with and without --atomic. The case requires API rejection for both attempts, a deployed rollback revision for the atomic trial, restored user values, and the same marker request afterward. An additive lifecycle branch rolls Cilium agents after a valid monitor-aggregation setting change, then observes a failed operator workload image rollout and explicit Helm rollback while keeping the agent datapath pinned. A case-owned namespaced CiliumNetworkPolicy permits only ordinary marker-client ingress to the marker-server TCP port, remains realized through the tested Helm lifecycle, and is removed afterward. This does not test a new Cilium version or failed agent datapath rollout, and does not assess production baseline, CVE status or patch timeliness, provider SLAs, RBAC process, PSA configuration, or production-scale availability.",
